This RED is a GENUINE MEANINGFUL EXECUTABLE tests-only failing result, captured through the
Cucumber Story BDD runner (not a direct-JUnit behavior test). It exercises the AC-FUNCTION-001
trailing-comment refinement scenario against production WITHOUT the packageEdit trailing-comment
fix. A compiler-proven public top-level Kotlin function whose source file carries a trailing line
comment on its package declaration ("package fixture.pricing // note") compiles cleanly
(compiler-proven), and the AC-FUNCTION-001 contract requires the preview to edit only the package
token while preserving every other source byte. Production refused it with
kotlin.movePackageDeclarationInvalid because packageEdit required an exact package line with no
trailing comment. This is a genuine production gap, captured BEFORE any production change, and
recorded here with the failing Cucumber command and observed exit/error.

The previous absence-only and direct-JUnit transcripts are superseded. The direct-JUnit behavior
test (KotlinJvmMoveTestsOnlyRedTest) was removed because direct hand-written JUnit behavior tests
are prohibited by the workflow; the executable RED below is the Cucumber-based replacement.

